  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Water Supply System Recovery For Upstream Communities Affected By The Kakhova Dam Breach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The breach of the Kakhovka Dam on 6 June 2023 led to massive flooding, causing significant infrastructural damage including to essential water, sanitation and heating systems. In the Pokrov community in the Dnipropetrovsk Oblast the breach caused a drop in water level and consequently a malfunctioning of the emergency power station, which has not allowed for the water to reach the treatment station serving the community. The proposed project therefore aims to contribute to the Pokrov community&#x2019;s improved access to reliable, sufficient, and safe water supply.</narrative>
  </description>
